id: decisions/023-state-ownership-in-interface
title: "A rendered page is never the record"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'state-ownership-in-interface'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: state-ownership-in-interface
axis_gloss: "whether the rendered surface owns the state it shows, or it is a derived projection of state owned elsewhere"
poles:
  a: model-holds-state
  b: view-holds-state
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 12
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(25) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Is a rendered page ever the record, or is every page a rebuildable view of a
  plain-text .yawn, and should the one route node that lists its HTML before its
  source be corrected?

why_it_matters: >
  Twenty-one authored statements say views never hold canonical state and the
  funnel bridge is forbidden from writing back into the source repo; one route
  node quietly lists index.html ahead of the .yawn it renders. A child Yawn that
  serves a public route inherits either 'source first, page rebuildable' or a
  precedent that the page may lead.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    24 judgments sit at model-holds-state (21 authored) and 1 at view-holds-state
    (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave intends holds: order to carry rank at all (the list-order
    decision); if not, this axis reduces to adding a source: key.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      A View never holds canonical state. Every route node lists its plain-text
      .yawn source before any rendered artifact under holds:, and every rendered
      artifact must be rebuildable from that source without loss.
    cost: "Swapping two lines in agency-declaration/node.yawn; one sentence added to core/folder-node.yawn node_shape."
    risk: "None beyond the edit; the funnel bridge already enforces the direction for the homepage."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A new test in tests/interface-contracts.test.mjs that walks every node.yawn and, for any holds: list containing an .html or other rendered artifact, asserts a .yawn entry precedes it."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0009"
      - "J0010"
      - "J0024"
      - "J0157"
      - "J0229"
      - "J0234"
  - name: B
    description: >
      A route node may name its rendered page as the primary object it holds; the
      .yawn beside it is a source note. The page is the record for that route.
    cost: "Rewriting core/projection-and-aperture.yawn invariants, the funnel-bridge source_repo_rule and the observation-view holon rule."
    risk: "Two canonical stores; a homepage edit that never reaches the protocol; every 'View, not canonical state' test breaks."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "There is no test on this side; adopting B means deleting 'serialization is a deterministic View materialization, not canonical state' from tests/observation-state-v1.test.mjs."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0796"
  - name: C
    description: >
      A View never holds canonical state, and holds: order in a node carries no
      rank; a route node names its canonical source under a separate source: key so
      the order of holds: is free.
    cost: "A source: key in agency-declaration/node.yawn; one sentence in core/folder-node.yawn."
    risk: "Depends on the list-order decision going the display-only way; otherwise two keys say the same thing."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Same walk as A, but asserting a source: key names a .yawn whenever holds: contains a rendered artifact."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0009"
      - "J0234"
      - "J0796"

recommendation:
  option_ref: A
  confidence: 0.85
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Every authored judgment is on A, three of them contract-defined and one
    (J0234) stating the rule three separate ways; the passing test 'serialization
    is a deterministic View materialization, not canonical state' implements it.
    The only exception is a two-line ordering in one node whose own purpose
    paragraph says the point is keeping the source declaration in plain text; the
    artifact orders it that way, nobody argued for it. Fix it and add the walk so
    it cannot recur. C is the fallback only if Dave decides list order carries no
    meaning anywhere.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "agency-declaration/node.yawn lists ../agency-declaration.yawn before index.html"
    - "A test in tests/ walks every node.yawn and rejects a holds: list where a rendered artifact precedes its .yawn source, and passes"
    - "core/folder-node.yawn node_shape says holds: names sources before renderings"

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A route's index.html is edited with content absent from its .yawn source and
    neither the funnel bridge nor a validator flags the drift.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0009"
  - "J0010"
  - "J0024"
  - "J0157"
  - "J0229"
  - "J0234"
  - "J0796"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
